{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["הבהמה — even though it parts the hoof, but the split is not fully cleft, such as a horse and a donkey. And does not bring up the cud — whoever touches them — whether dead or slaughtered [becomes impure]. And here it did not specify in their dying, but regarding a clean animal it wrote before us: ״וכי ימות מן הבהמה אשר היא לכם לאכלה״ and so on — specifically when dead, but slaughtered it is clean, and even a טריפה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:39.588517147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}